<article class="problem-card">

<div class="problem-header">

<div class="problem-number">
PROBLEM 03
</div>

<h2>
Attractive finite square well
</h2>

</div>


<section class="section">

<div class="section-title">
Question Statement
</div>

<p>
Solve the Schrödinger equation for
</p>

<div class="equation">

\[
V(x)=
\begin{cases}
0,&x<0,\\
-V_0,&0<x<a,\\
0,&x>a,
\end{cases}
\]

</div>

<p>
where V_0>0 and E>0.
Particles are incident from x=-\infty.
Express all coefficients in terms of one common coefficient.
</p>

</section>


<section class="section">

<div class="section-title">
Concept
</div>

<p>
Outside the well:
</p>

<div class="equation">

\[
\boxed{
k=
\frac{\sqrt{2mE}}{\hbar}
}
\]

</div>

<p>
Inside the attractive well:
</p>

<div class="equation">

\[
\boxed{
q=
\frac{\sqrt{2m(E+V_0)}}{\hbar}
}
\]

</div>

<p>
Since V_0>0,
</p>

<div class="equation">

\[
q>k.
\]

</div>

</section>


<section class="section">

<div class="section-title">
Complete Solution
</div>


<div class="step">

<h4>Region I: x<0</h4>

<div class="equation">

\[
\psi_1=Ae^{ikx}+Be^{-ikx}
\]

</div>

</div>


<div class="step">

<h4>Region II: 0<x<a</h4>

<div class="equation">

\[
\psi_2=Ce^{iqx}+De^{-iqx}
\]

</div>

</div>


<div class="step">

<h4>Region III: x>a</h4>

<div class="equation">

\[
\psi_3=Fe^{ikx}
\]

</div>

</div>


<div class="step">

<h4>Boundary conditions at x=0</h4>

<div class="equation">

\[
A+B=C+D
\]

\[
k(A-B)=q(C-D)
\]

</div>

</div>


<div class="step">

<h4>Boundary conditions at x=a</h4>

<div class="equation">

\[
Ce^{iqa}+De^{-iqa}=Fe^{ika}
\]

\[
q(Ce^{iqa}-De^{-iqa})
=
kFe^{ika}
\]

</div>

</div>


<div class="step">

<h4>Choose F=F_0</h4>

<div class="equation">

\[
\boxed{
C=
F_0e^{i(k-q)a}
\frac{k+q}{2q}
}
\]

\[
\boxed{
D=
F_0e^{i(k+q)a}
\frac{q-k}{2q}
}
\]

</div>

<p>
Using the x=0 conditions:
</p>

<div class="equation">

\[
\boxed{
A=
F_0e^{ika}
\left[
\cos(qa)
-i\frac{k^2+q^2}{2kq}\sin(qa)
\right]
}
\]

\[
\boxed{
B=
iF_0e^{ika}
\frac{q^2-k^2}{2kq}\sin(qa)
}
\]

</div>

<div class="final-equation">

\[
\boxed{
F=F_0
}
\]

</div>

</div>

</section>


<div class="physics-box">

<h3>Physical Interpretation</h3>

<p>
The attractive well increases the kinetic energy of the particle
inside the well. Hence q>k, meaning that the wavelength inside
the well is shorter than outside.
</p>

</div>

</article>



