<article class="problem-card">

<div class="problem-header">

<div class="problem-number">
PROBLEM 05
</div>

<h2>
The half harmonic oscillator
</h2>

</div>


<section class="section">

<div class="section-title">
Question Statement
</div>

<p>
Find the solution to the half harmonic oscillator and compare its
energy values and wave functions with those of the full harmonic
oscillator.
</p>

</section>


<section class="section">

<div class="section-title">
Concept
</div>

<div class="equation">

\[
V(x)=
\begin{cases}
\infty,&x<0,\\
\dfrac12kx^2,&x>0.
\end{cases}
\]

</div>

<p>
For the full oscillator:
</p>

<div class="equation">

\[
\boxed{
E_n=
\hbar\omega
\left(
n+\frac12
\right)
}
\]

</div>

<p>
The infinite wall requires
</p>

<div class="final-equation">

\[
\boxed{\psi(0)=0}
\]

</div>

</section>


<section class="section">

<div class="section-title">
Complete Solution
</div>


<div class="step">

<h4>Full oscillator wave functions</h4>

<div class="equation">

\[
\psi_n(x)
=
\frac{1}{\sqrt{2^n n!}}
\left(
\frac{\alpha}{\sqrt{\pi}}
\right)^{1/2}
H_n(\alpha x)
e^{-\alpha^2x^2/2}
\]

</div>

<div class="equation">

\[
\alpha=
\sqrt{\frac{m\omega}{\hbar}}.
\]

</div>

</div>


<div class="step">

<h4>Even states</h4>

<p>
For n=0,2,4,\ldots, the wave functions are even:
</p>

<div class="equation">

\[
\psi_n(-x)=\psi_n(x).
\]

</div>

<p>
Generally \psi_n(0)\neq0, so they violate the wall condition.
They are therefore excluded.
</p>

</div>


<div class="step">

<h4>Odd states</h4>

<p>
For n=1,3,5,\ldots:
</p>

<div class="equation">

\[
\psi_n(-x)=-\psi_n(x)
\]

</div>

<p>
so
</p>

<div class="equation">

\[
\psi_n(0)=0.
\]

</div>

<p>
Therefore the odd states survive.
</p>

</div>


<div class="step">

<h4>Allowed energies</h4>

<p>
Put
</p>

<div class="equation">

\[
n=2r+1.
\]

</div>

<p>
Then:
</p>

<div class="final-equation">

\[
\boxed{
E_r=
\left(
2r+\frac32
\right)\hbar\omega
}
\]

</div>

<p>
Thus:
</p>

<div class="equation">

\[
\boxed{
\frac32\hbar\omega,\quad
\frac72\hbar\omega,\quad
\frac{11}{2}\hbar\omega,\quad
\frac{15}{2}\hbar\omega,\ldots
}
\]

</div>


<div class="step">

<h4>Half-oscillator wave functions</h4>

<div class="final-equation">

\[
\boxed{
\psi_r^{(\mathrm{half})}(x)
=
\sqrt2\,
\psi_{2r+1}^{(\mathrm{full})}(x),
\qquad x>0
}
\]

</div>

<p>
and
</p>

<div class="equation">

\[
\psi(x)=0,
\qquad x\le0.
\]

</div>

</div>

</section>


<div class="physics-box">

<h3>Physical Interpretation</h3>

<p>
The wall imposes \psi(0)=0. Only the full harmonic-oscillator
states that already have a node at x=0 satisfy this condition.
Therefore odd states survive and even states disappear.
</p>

</div>

</article>



