<article class="problem-card">

<div class="problem-header">

<div class="problem-number">
PROBLEM 07
</div>

<h2>
Ground-state uncertainty of the harmonic oscillator
</h2>

</div>


<section class="section">

<div class="section-title">
Question Statement
</div>

<p>
For the ground state of the one-dimensional simple harmonic oscillator:
</p>

<ul>

<li>Find \langle x\rangle and \langle x^2\rangle.</li>

<li>Find \Delta x.</li>

<li>Find \langle p_x\rangle and \langle p_x^2\rangle.</li>

<li>Find \Delta p_x and \Delta x\Delta p_x.</li>

</ul>

</section>


<section class="section">

<div class="section-title">
Concept
</div>

<div class="equation">

\[
\boxed{
\psi_0(x)
=
\left(
\frac{\alpha}{\sqrt{\pi}}
\right)^{1/2}
e^{-\alpha^2x^2/2}
}
\]

</div>

<div class="equation">

\[
\boxed{
\alpha=
\sqrt{\frac{m\omega}{\hbar}}
}
\]

</div>

</section>


<section class="section">

<div class="section-title">
Complete Solution
</div>


<div class="step">

<h4>(a) \langle x\rangle</h4>

<div class="equation">

\[
\langle x\rangle
=
\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}
\psi_0^*x\psi_0\,dx.
\]

</div>

<p>
The probability density is even while x is odd.
Therefore the integrand is odd:
</p>

<div class="final-equation">

\[
\boxed{
\langle x\rangle=0
}
\]

</div>

</div>


<div class="step">

<h4>\langle x^2\rangle</h4>

<div class="equation">

\[
\langle x^2\rangle
=
\int_{-\infty}^{\infty}
x^2|\psi_0|^2dx
\]

</div>

<div class="final-equation">

\[
\boxed{
\langle x^2\rangle
=
\frac{1}{2\alpha^2}
=
\frac{\hbar}{2m\omega}
}
\]

</div>

</div>


<div class="step">

<h4>(b) \Delta x</h4>

<div class="equation">

\[
\Delta x
=
\sqrt{
\langle x^2\rangle
-
\langle x\rangle^2
}
\]

</div>

<div class="final-equation">

\[
\boxed{
\Delta x=
\sqrt{
\frac{\hbar}{2m\omega}
}
}
\]

</div>

</div>


<div class="step">

<h4>(c) Momentum expectation values</h4>

<div class="equation">

\[
\hat p_x
=
-i\hbar\frac{d}{dx}
\]

</div>

<p>
Because the ground state is real and symmetric:
</p>

<div class="final-equation">

\[
\boxed{
\langle p_x\rangle=0
}
\]

</div>

<p>
The ground-state energy is:
</p>

<div class="equation">

\[
E_0=\frac12\hbar\omega.
\]

</div>

<p>
The average potential energy is:
</p>

<div class="equation">

\[
\langle V\rangle
=
\frac12m\omega^2
\langle x^2\rangle
\]

</div>

<div class="equation">

\[
\langle V\rangle
=
\frac12m\omega^2
\frac{\hbar}{2m\omega}
=
\frac14\hbar\omega.
\]

</div>

<p>
Therefore:
</p>

<div class="equation">

\[
\langle K\rangle
=
E_0-\langle V\rangle
\]

\[
=
\frac12\hbar\omega
-
\frac14\hbar\omega
\]

\[
\boxed{
\langle K\rangle=
\frac14\hbar\omega
}
\]

</div>

<p>
Since K=p_x^2/2m:
</p>

<div class="final-equation">

\[
\boxed{
\langle p_x^2\rangle
=
\frac12m\hbar\omega
}
\]

</div>

</div>


<div class="step">

<h4>(d) \Delta p_x</h4>

<div class="equation">

\[
\Delta p_x
=
\sqrt{
\langle p_x^2\rangle
-
\langle p_x\rangle^2
}
\]

</
